"he","קֵרַ֤בְתִּי",null,"H7126","HVpp1cs"],["he","צִדְקָתִי֙",null,"H6666","HNcfsc/Sp1cs"],["he","לֹ֣א",null,"H3808","HTn"],["he","תִרְחָ֔ק",null,"H7368","HVqi3fs"],["he","וּתְשׁוּעָתִ֖י",null,"H8668","HC/Ncfsc/Sp1cs","c"],["he","לֹ֣א",null,"H3808","HTn"],["he","תְאַחֵ֑ר",null,"H309","HVpi3fs"],["he","וְנָתַתִּ֤י",null,"H5414","HC/Vqq1cs","c"],["he","בְצִיּוֹן֙",null,"H6726","HR/Np","b"],["he","תְּשׁוּעָ֔ה",null,"H8668","HNcfsa"],["he","לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל",null,"H3478","HR/Np","l"],["he","תִּפְאַרְתִּֽי",null,"H8597","HNcfsc/Sp1cs"]]},"gl":{"H3766":"to bow","H1078":"Bel","H7164":"to stoop","H5015":"Nebo","H1961":"to be","H6091":"idol","H2416":"alive","H929":"animal","H5385":"burden","H6006":"to lift","H4853":"burden","H5889":"faint","H3162":"unitedness","H3808":"not","H3201":"be able","H4422":"to escape","H5315":"soul","H7628":"captivity","H1980":"went","H8085":"hear","H413":"to(wards)","H1004":"place","H3290":"Jacob","H3605":"all","H7611":"remnant","H3478":"Israel","H4480":"from","H990":"abdomen","H5375":"raise","H7356":"womb","H5704":"till","H2209":"old age","H589":"I","H1931":"he/she/it","H7872":"greyheaded","H5445":"to bear","H6213":"do","H4310":"who?","H1819":"to resemble","H7737":"be like","H4911":"to liken","H2107":"to lavish/despise","H2091":"gold","H3599":"purse","H3701":"money","H7070":"branch","H8254":"to weigh","H7936":"to hire","H6884":"to refine","H410":"God","H5456":"to prostrate","H637":"also","H7812":"to bow","H5921":"upon","H3802":"shoulder","H3240":"to rest","H8478":"under","H5975":"stand","H4725":"place","H4185":"to remove","H6817":"to cry","H6030":"to dwell","H6869":"dearth","H3467":"to save","H2142":"to remember","H2063":"this","H377":"be manly","H7725":"return","H6586":"to transgress","H3820":"heart","H7223":"first","H5769":"enduring","H3588":"for","H595":"I","H369":"nothing","H5750":"still","H430":"God","H657":"end","H3644":"like","H5046":"to tell","H7225":"beginning","H319":"end","H6924":"East","H834":"which","H559":"to say","H6098":"counsel","H6965":"(Leb)-kamai","H2656":"pleasure","H7121":"call to","H4217":"East (Gate)","H5861":"bird of prey","H776":"country/planet","H4801":"distance","H376":"man","H1696":"speak","H935":"come","H3335":"formed","H47":"ox","H7350":"distant","H6666":"righteousness","H7126":"come","H7368":"to remove","H8668":"salvation","H309":"to delay","H5414":"give","H6726":"Zion","H8597":"beauty"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"cyril-alexandria","Bel; perhaps Nimrod, (Calmet) or Saturn, to whom they sacrificed their children. (Worthington) — Nabo, “the oracle” of Belus. The Chaldeans adored statues and beasts. But the Persians worshipped the elements. (Calmet) — Xerxes destroyed the tomb of Belus, after his expedition into Greece. (Arrian vii.) He had there demolished the temples, (Herodotus viii. 109.) pretending (Haydock) that “the world is the house of the gods.” (Cicero, Leg. ii.) — Weariness. The priests affected to be weighed down, as if the god were present. (Baruch vi. 25.) (St. Cyril)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","They. Literally, “their soul.” (Haydock) — The pagans must have supposed they had one. (Calmet) — Captivity. “There are as many triumphs over the gods as over men.” (Tertullian) — The former shared the fate of their adorers. Their statues were plundered."],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","By my. Vulgate may have read a me ab, (Calmet) instead of a meo. Hebrew and Septuagint, “taken from the womb,” (Haydock) and treated with the utmost tenderness. (Calmet)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Ashamed. Septuagint, “groan.” Protestants, “shew yourselves men.” (Haydock)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Bird; Cyrus, whose rapid conquests are thus denoted. (Calmet) — He chose a golden eagle, with wings expanded, for his standard. (Xenophon vii.) — Christ came from heaven to redeem the world, Psalm xviii. 6., and Malachias iv. 2. (Calmet) — He was the orient, adored by the eastern sages, to whom the prophet refers. (St. Jerome) (Worthington)"],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Israel. It shall no longer be a reproach. Cyrus shall restore my people to their own country. But Christ more full accomplished what is here declared respecting the establishment of his Church. (Calmet)"]],"au":{"cyril-alexandria":["Cyril of Alexandria",1,1,444,"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/#cyril"],"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]},"fa":[[8,null,0,"Tractates on the Gospel of John","Tractate 18",0,430,"… We return perhaps to ourselves, if we are not the trangressors to whom it is said, \"Return, O trangressors, to your heart. Return to your heart: why go from yourselves, and perish from yourselves? Why go the ways of solitude? You go astray by wandering: return ye. Whither? To the Lord. 'Tis quickly done: first return to thine own heart; thou hast wandered abroad an exile from thyself; thou knowest not thyself, and yet thou art asking by whom thou wast made! Return, return to thy heart, lift thyself away from the body: thy body is thy place of abode; thy heart perceives even by thy body. …"]],"fau":[["augustine","Augustine of Hippo",1,"father",null,1,430]],"ftr":[["Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers, series 1, vol. 7 (1888)","https://ccel.org/ccel/schaff/npnf107"]]}